# server must return index.html for anything that is not a real file rather
# than a 404.
#
# Without this, every deep link breaks on a static host — a client opening
# /public/schedule/Lorablooms, a staff member opening a /contract/... link from
# their email, or anyone refreshing a page that is not "/". The Lovable host
# does this implicitly; Cloudflare Pages and Netlify need it written down.
